# Git workflow (Berth)

## Branches

| Branch | Role |
|--------|------|
| `main` | Default — orchestrator-verified roadmap commits land here |
| `orchestrator/P<phase>[-T<nn>]` | Lane P worktree branches — merged to `main` after verify |

- Lane P agents use **Cursor git worktrees** (`subagent_type: "best-of-n-runner"`), not shared-checkout branch switching.
- **Never push** unless the user explicitly asks.

## Commit messages (Conventional Commits)

Subject ≤72 chars, imperative mood, **scoped**. **Orchestrator task commits must link the work item.**

```
feat(<scope>)[P6]: <imperative summary>        # roadmap phase
feat(<scope>)[P0-T03]: <summary>               # roadmap sub-task
fix(<scope>)[#12]: <summary>                  # GitLab issue (post-MVP)
```

**Roadmap:** `[P<phase>[-T<nn>]]` in subject; `Task: P<phase>[-T<nn>]` on its own line in the body.

**GitHub issue (bugs/iteration):** `[#N]` in subject; `fixes #N` in body. **Never** Kaneo task IDs — see `03-issue-commit-linking.mdc`.

**Allowed scopes:** `repo`, `ci`, `api`, `web`, `db`, `docker`, `docs`, `deps`, `auth`, `registry`

## Commit rules

- **Orchestrator execution sub-agents MUST commit** before verifier handoff — one task = **one implementation commit**. Overrides generic "only commit when asked" for orchestrator-dispatched work.
- **Never** `git add .` or `git add -A`. Stage explicit paths from WRITE SCOPE (+ generated migrations / lockfile when applicable).
- Never amend commits that have been pushed.

## Push policy

**Never push** unless the user explicitly asks. Run full CI before push when requested.

## Example

```bash
git add docker/compose.yml app/api/health/route.ts
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
feat(docker)[P0]: add three-service compose skeleton

Task: P0
EOF
)"
```
